  // ⚠️ VarChar(16), NOT 10 (#1028, 2026-09-30). `STRONG_SELL` is ELEVEN characters, so at
  // VarChar(10) MySQL truncated it to `STRONG_SEL` on write — 1,081 rows of real scoring history
  // were stored as a value that is not a signal class at all. Measured: `STRONG_BUY` (10) fitted
  // EXACTLY, which is why the defect hid — only the bearish strong class was corrupted, and only
  // the highest-conviction bearish signal the system can produce.
  tradingSignal String @map("trading_signal") @db.VarChar(16)
  rarityPct  Float?
  signalPct  Float?   // #726 — pre-gate directional % (the "signal %" a user sees)
